THOUGHT: I can see that `defaultOptions()` does indeed call `defaultTypeParsers()` to populate `FuncMap`. So the parsers for `url.URL` and `time.Location` should be available. Let me create a test script to reproduce the issue and see what's happening:

```bash
cat <<'EOF' > test_issue.go
package main

import (
    "fmt"
    "net/url"
    "time"

    "github.com/caarlos0/env/v11"
)

type Config struct {
    ExampleURL  url.URL       `env:"EXAMPLE_URL"`
    Location    time.Location `env:"LOCATION"`
}

func main() {
    cfg := Config{}
    if err := env.Parse(&cfg); err != nil {
        fmt.Printf("Error: %v\n", err)
    } else {
        fmt.Printf("Success: URL=%s, Location=%s\n", cfg.ExampleURL.String(), cfg.Location.String())
    }
}
EOF
```

